LAST-MODIFIED:20260416T122401Z
UID:38173-1781807400-1781812800@apostlesucc.org
SUMMARY:Mocktails & Meaning™: Racial Equity Demographics in Lancaster County
DESCRIPTION:Step into an evening of learning and reflection at our June Mocktails & Meaning™ session on June 18th at 6:30 PM\, featuring the YWCA of Lancaster and a focused look at Racial Equity Demographics of Lancaster County. This conversation will explore the data behind our community—highlighting disparities\, trends\, and opportunities for growth—while inviting us to consider how we can be more informed\, engaged\, and equity-minded neighbors. Sip on a refreshing Grapefruit Paloma mocktail 🍊🍹 as we engage in meaningful dialogue and deepen our understanding together. Please note that due to ongoing renovations\, seating is limited\, so we encourage you to register early. Mocktails & Meaning™ will pause for the summer after this session and return in the fall. \nRegister Now by Clicking Here
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/mocktails-meaning-racial-equity-demographics-in-lancaster-county/
LOCATION:Church of the Apostles UCC\, 1850 Marietta Ave\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Mocktails-Meaning-Flyer-Banner-Landscape-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
